Legacy code is monolithic in nature. 
- Single unit of deployment
- Running as a single service. 
- Low fault tolerance with scaling limitations
- Lock into a particular technology stack
- Common libraries to many applications

Container 
- Standardised unit for development, deployment and distribution of application
- Programming language runtimes
- Executables, binary code, libraries and config files.
- Immutable, does not change once its built. 
- Runs as a single Unix process.
- Disposable and safe to scale up/down at anytime

Containers vs Virtual Machines
- Management layer -> Hypervisor for VMS, Container run time for Containers

Docker Runtime
- Docker Enginer
- Container runtime
- long running server process aka Docker Daemon. dockerd, in unix
- Commands REST API to Docker RUNTIME	

