Exposing docker containers
- Containers have port too.
- docker container run -d -p 8080:80 (8080 is localhost directs to container port 80) httpd
 
Creating an Image
- Config file using Dockerfile, then use 'docker build'
- FROM specify base image, first instruction on the dockerfile
- COPY copies everything from a specified directory to a destination directory
- WORKDIR go to specified directory
- CMD default command that runs when starting the container
- 'docker image build . -t image_name:image_tag'
- Dont use latest tag, have a certain naming standardisation
